:":†~ç◊À‚YE÷1¥óÎ⁄≠˝␀␀ˇˇB$l·å,ß◊␀␀␀ˇˇ␀s(Íé␀,7:headers;1681:40:4:Date,29:Mon, 06 Apr 2026 09:50:52 GMT,]52:12:Content-Type,32:text/event-stream; charset=utf-8,]31:17:Transfer-Encoding,7:chunked,]28:10:Connection,10:keep-alive,]28:13:Cache-Control,8:no-cache,]52:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-limit,7:2000000,]56:42:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-remaining,7:1956000,]66:38:anthropic-ratelimit-input-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T09:50:52Z,]52:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-limit,6:400000,]56:43:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-remaining,6:400000,]67:39:anthropic-ratelimit-output-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T09:50:50Z,]45:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-limit,4:4000,]49:38:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-remaining,4:3999,]62:34:anthropic-ratelimit-requests-reset,20:2026-04-06T09:50:50Z,]46:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-limit,7:2400000,]50:36:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-remaining,7:2356000,]60:32:anthropic-ratelimit-tokens-reset,20:2026-04-06T09:50:50Z,]46:10:request-id,28:req_011CZnJxMUYAQaoFDs1HJsCq,]77:25:strict-transport-security,44:max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload,]69:25:anthropic-organization-id,36:19d39eaa-efb4-49e0-afe8-a7359703719a,]23:6:Server,10:cloudflare,]40:29:x-envoy-upstream-service-time,4:1774,]27:16:Content-Encoding,4:gzip,]26:4:vary,15:Accept-Encoding,]46:13:server-timing,25:x-originResponse;dur=1777,]208:10:set-cookie,189:_cfuvid=l4g3SAQ0seeHI9UUZ55zBKhaW7UCB8JTeYOjhu1uaGI-1775469050.4747858-1.0.1.1-ar1V8B3uPMvKRrVdzRqUIL3es6YC55LSNpTwJeA.XDI; HttpOnly; SameSite=None; Secure; Path=/; Domain=api.anthropic.com,]23:12:X-Robots-Tag,4:none,]29:15:cf-cache-status,7:DYNAMIC,]73:23:Content-Security-Policy,42:default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none',]33:6:CF-RAY,20:9e7fe3fd7f286a60-DUB,]]12:http_version;8:HTTP/1.1,}7:request;230398:4:path;22:/v1/messages?beta=true,9:authority;0:,6:scheme;5:https,6:method;4:POST,4:port;3:443#4:host;17:api.anthropic.com;13:timestamp_end;18:1775469050.4170437^15:timestamp_start;18:1775469050.4155924^8:trailers;0:~7:content;229130:{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are available for use with the Skill tool:\n\n- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so m‚Ä¶\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo, defaults to 10m) - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep‚Ä¶\n- claude-api: Build apps with the Claude API or Anthropic SDK.\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`/`claude_agent_sdk`, or user asks to use Claude API, Anthropic SDKs, or Agent SDK.\nDO NOT TRIGGER when: code imports `openai`/other AI SDK, ge‚Ä¶\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nPlan mode is active. The user indicated that they do not want you to execute yet -- you MUST NOT make any edits (with the exception of the plan file mentioned below), run any non-readonly tools (including changing configs or making commits), or otherwise make any changes to the system. This supercedes any other instructions you have received.\n\n## Plan File Info:\nNo plan file exists yet. You should create your plan at /root/.claude/plans/cuddly-bubbling-whale.md using the Write tool.\nYou should build your plan incrementally by writing to or editing this file. NOTE that this is the only file you are allowed to edit - other than this you are only allowed to take READ-ONLY actions.\n\n## Plan Workflow\n\n### Phase 1: Initial Understanding\nGoal: Gain a comprehensive understanding of the user's request by reading through code and asking them questions. Critical: In this phase you should only use the Explore subagent type.\n\n1. Focus on understanding the user's request and the code associated with their request. Actively search for existing functions, utilities, and patterns that can be reused ‚Äî avoid proposing new code when suitable implementations already exist.\n\n2. **Launch up to 3 Explore agents IN PARALLEL** (single message, multiple tool calls) to efficiently explore the codebase.\n   - Use 1 agent when the task is isolated to known files, the user provided specific file paths, or you're making a small targeted change.\n   - Use multiple agents when: the scope is uncertain, multiple areas of the codebase are involved, or you need to understand existing patterns before planning.\n   - Quality over quantity - 3 agents maximum, but you should try to use the minimum number of agents necessary (usually just 1)\n   - If using multiple agents: Provide each agent with a specific search focus or area to explore. Example: One agent searches for existing implementations, another explores related components, a third investigating testing patterns\n\n### Phase 2: Design\nGoal: Design an implementation approach.\n\nLaunch Plan agent(s) to design the implementation based on the user's intent and your exploration results from Phase 1.\n\nYou can launch up to 1 agent(s) in parallel.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- **Default**: Launch at least 1 Plan agent for most tasks - it helps validate your understanding and consider alternatives\n- **Skip agents**: Only for truly trivial tasks (typo fixes, single-line changes, simple renames)\n\nIn the agent prompt:\n- Provide comprehensive background context from Phase 1 exploration including filenames and code path traces\n- Describe requirements and constraints\n- Request a detailed implementation plan\n\n### Phase 3: Review\nGoal: Review the plan(s) from Phase 2 and ensure alignment with the user's intentions.\n1. Read the critical files identified by agents to deepen your understanding\n2. Ensure that the plans align with the user's original request\n3. Use AskUserQuestion to clarify any remaining questions with the user\n\n### Phase 4: Final Plan\nGoal: Write your final plan to the plan file (the only file you can edit).\n- Begin with a **Context** section: explain why this change is being made ‚Äî the problem or need it addresses, what prompted it, and the intended outcome\n- Include only your recommended approach, not all alternatives\n- Ensure that the plan file is concise enough to scan quickly, but detailed enough to execute effectively\n- Include the paths of critical files to be modified\n- Reference existing functions and utilities you found that should be reused, with their file paths\n- Include a verification section describing how to test the changes end-to-end (run the code, use MCP tools, run tests)\n\n### Phase 5: Call ExitPlanMode\nAt the very end of your turn, once you have asked the user questions and are happy with your final plan file - you should always call ExitPlanMode to indicate to the user that you are done planning.\nThis is critical - your turn should only end with either using the AskUserQuestion tool OR calling ExitPlanMode. Do not stop unless it's for these 2 reasons\n\n**Important:** Use AskUserQuestion ONLY to clarify requirements or choose between approaches. Use ExitPlanMode to request plan approval. Do NOT ask about plan approval in any other way - no text questions, no AskUserQuestion. Phrases like \"Is this plan okay?\", \"Should I proceed?\", \"How does this plan look?\", \"Any changes before we start?\", or similar MUST use ExitPlanMode.\n\nNOTE: At any point in time through this workflow you should feel free to ask the user questions or clarifications using the AskUserQuestion tool. Don't make large assumptions about user intent. The goal is to present a well researched plan to the user, and tie any loose ends before implementation begins.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-04-06.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"# LRU File Cache ‚Äî Swift Spec\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Disk-backed LRU cache for iOS\n- Support multiple independent named caches (e.g. images, videos), each with their own configuration\n- Fast start: cache must be usable immediately after init with no blocking I/O on the hot path\n- LRU order is determined by last-accessed date\n- Eviction runs asynchronously and must not block reads or writes\n- Eviction moves files to the system `tmp/` directory rather than deleting them; file name collisions in `tmp/` must be handled\n- All insertions use atomic writes\n- The index (LRU metadata) is persisted to disk and survives process restarts\n\n## Configuration (per cache)\n\n- Name (used as the on-disk namespace)\n- Max entry count\n- Max total byte size\n- Eviction debounce interval\n- iOS data protection class\n\n## API\n\n| Method | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `add(key, data)` | Insert a new entry; replace if key already exists |\n| `update(key, data)` | Alias for `add`; signals update intent to the caller |\n| `modify(key, data)` | Replace payload for an existing key; error if key is absent |\n| `get(key)` | Return payload and bump last-accessed date; return nil if absent |\n| `promote(key)` | Update last-accessed date without reading the payload; error if key is absent |\n\n## Constraints\n\n- `modify` must fail explicitly if the key does not exist; `add` and `update` must not\n- `get` and `promote` both count as an access and must update LRU order\n- Index persistence triggered by `get`/`promote` should be debounced to avoid write amplification\n- Index persistence triggered by mutations (`add`, `modify`, eviction) must be immediate\n- A cache directory deleted externally must be recreated on next write\n- A corrupted index on init must degrade gracefully to an empty cache, not a crash\n- A file present in the index but missing on disk at `get` time must return nil and self-heal the index\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012s2vKD5Szca2moyagMH5zM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Explore workspace structure","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Explore the workspace at /workspace. I need to understand:\n1. What files and directories exist\n2. If there's any existing Swift code, Package.swift, or Xcode project files\n3. Any existing cache-related code\n4. Any test files or test infrastructure\n\nReport the full directory structure and contents of any Swift files found."}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012s2vKD5Szca2moyagMH5zM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. Now I have a complete picture of the workspace. Let me provide you with a comprehensive report:\n\n## Workspace Exploration Report\n\n### Directory Structure\n\nThe workspace at `/workspace` is currently **empty of user files**. The only content is a git repository with a minimal history.\n\n```\n/workspace\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ .git/\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ COMMIT_EDITMSG\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ HEAD\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ config\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ description\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ index\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ branches/\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ hooks/ (standard git hooks - all samples)\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ info/\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ logs/\n‚îÇ   ‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ HEAD\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ objects/\n‚îÇ   ‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ (minimal git objects)\n‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ refs/\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ heads/\n‚îÇ       ‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ master\n‚îÇ       ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ tags/\n‚îÇ           ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ eval-baseline\n```\n\n### Git Repository State\n\n- **Current branch**: master\n- **Working tree**: Clean (nothing to commit)\n- **Commits**: Only 1 commit - \"initial (empty workspace)\"\n- **Tags**: eval-baseline (pointing to same initial commit)\n- **Files tracked**: None (the repository is completely empty)\n\n### Swift Files and Project Files\n\n**Result: No Swift files found**\n- ‚úó No `.swift` files\n- ‚úó No `Package.swift` (Swift Package Manager manifest)\n- ‚úó No `.xcodeproj` directories (Xcode projects)\n- ‚úó No `.xcworkspace` files\n\n### Cache-Related Code\n\n**Result: No cache code found**\n- ‚úó No Swift source files to analyze\n- ‚úó No build artifacts or caches\n\n### Test Files/Infrastructure\n\n**Result: No test infrastructure found**\n- ‚úó No test files\n- ‚úó No test frameworks or configurations\n- ‚úó No README or documentation files\n\n### Summary\n\nThe workspace is a freshly initialized git repository with **no actual project files**. It's ready for new content to be added. There is currently:\n- No existing Swift code\n- No project configuration files\n- No test infrastructure\n- No cache implementations or related code\n\nThe repository appears to be a blank slate awaiting initial project setup and implementation."}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JCpuDo9Ch4cMv1o9nr6ooL","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design LRU cache implementation plan","subagent_type":"Plan","prompt":"Design a detailed Swift Package Manager implementation plan for a disk-backed LRU file cache for iOS. The workspace is empty ‚Äî we're starting from scratch.\n\n## Requirements\n\n### Core Features\n- Disk-backed LRU cache for iOS\n- Support multiple independent named caches (e.g. images, videos), each with their own configuration\n- Fast start: cache must be usable immediately after init with no blocking I/O on the hot path\n- LRU order is determined by last-accessed date\n- Eviction runs asynchronously and must not block reads or writes\n- Eviction moves files to the system `tmp/` directory rather than deleting them; file name collisions in `tmp/` must be handled\n- All insertions use atomic writes\n- The index (LRU metadata) is persisted to disk and survives process restarts\n\n### Configuration (per cache)\n- Name (used as the on-disk namespace)\n- Max entry count\n- Max total byte size\n- Eviction debounce interval\n- iOS data protection class\n\n### API\n| Method | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `add(key, data)` | Insert a new entry; replace if key already exists |\n| `update(key, data)` | Alias for `add`; signals update intent to the caller |\n| `modify(key, data)` | Replace payload for an existing key; error if key is absent |\n| `get(key)` | Return payload and bump last-accessed date; return nil if absent |\n| `promote(key)` | Update last-accessed date without reading the payload; error if key is absent |\n\n### Constraints\n- `modify` must fail explicitly if the key does not exist; `add` and `update` must not\n- `get` and `promote` both count as an access and must update LRU order\n- Index persistence triggered by `get`/`promote` should be debounced to avoid write amplification\n- Index persistence triggered by mutations (`add`, `modify`, eviction) must be immediate\n- A cache directory deleted externally must be recreated on next write\n- A corrupted index on init must degrade gracefully to an empty cache, not a crash\n- A file present in the index but missing on disk at `get` time must return nil and self-heal the index\n\n## Design Decisions to Address\n\n1. **File Structure**: How to organize files on disk (directory structure, naming scheme for cache entries)\n2. **Index Format**: What format to persist the LRU index (JSON, Codable struct, etc.)\n3. **Concurrency**: How to handle thread safety for reads/writes/eviction ‚Äî use actors, serial queues, or locks?\n4. **Atomic Writes**: Mechanism for atomic writes on iOS\n5. **Eviction Debounce**: Mechanism for debouncing eviction\n6. **Index Persistence Debounce**: Mechanism for debouncing index saves on get/promote\n7. **Error Types**: Define a clear error enum\n8. **Testing**: How to structure tests with Swift Testing or XCTest\n\n## Output Required\n\nProduce a detailed plan covering:\n1. Swift Package structure (sources, tests, targets)\n2. File layout (which Swift files, what each contains)\n3. All types/structs/classes/actors needed with their responsibilities\n4. Key algorithms (LRU eviction logic, atomic write mechanism, debounce mechanism)\n5. The index data model (what fields are stored per entry)\n6. Concurrency model in detail\n7. Test strategy\n8. File naming conventions for cache entries on disk"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JCpuDo9Ch4cMv1o9nr6ooL","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The workspace is completely empty. This is a greenfield Swift package. Let me now design the full implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n# Swift Package Manager: Disk-Backed LRU File Cache for iOS\n\n## 1. Swift Package Structure\n\n### Package Layout\n\n```\nDiskCache/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Package.swift\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ README.md\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Sources/\n‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCache/\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCache.swift              # Public entry point / facade\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheConfiguration.swift    # Per-cache config value type\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheError.swift            # Error enum\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheIndex.swift            # In-memory index + Codable model\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheEntry.swift            # Per-entry metadata model\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheActor.swift            # Swift actor: all mutable state\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ EvictionPolicy.swift        # LRU eviction algorithm\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriter.swift          # Atomic write via tmp + rename\n‚îÇ       ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Debouncer.swift             # Generic debounce helper\n‚îÇ       ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ FileProtectionMapper.swift  # Maps config enum ‚Üí FileProtection\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Tests/\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCacheTests/\n        ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCacheTests.swift         # Core API tests\n        ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ EvictionTests.swift          # LRU ordering and eviction tests\n        ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ PersistenceTests.swift       # Index survive-restart tests\n        ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ ConcurrencyTests.swift       # Actor isolation / race tests\n        ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriterTests.swift      # Atomic write correctness\n        ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Helpers/\n            ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ TestCacheFactory.swift   # Creates temp-dir-backed caches\n```\n\n### `Package.swift` Targets\n\n```swift\n// swift-tools-version: 5.9\ntargets: [\n    .target(\n        name: \"DiskCache\",\n        path: \"Sources/DiskCache\",\n        swiftSettings: [.enableExperimentalFeature(\"StrictConcurrency\")]\n    ),\n    .testTarget(\n        name: \"DiskCacheTests\",\n        dependencies: [\"DiskCache\"],\n        path: \"Tests/DiskCacheTests\"\n    )\n]\n```\n\nThe minimum platform is iOS 16 (to guarantee `actor` support and `FileProtection` APIs). Swift 5.9 is the minimum toolchain to enable strict concurrency checking and `~Copyable` if needed later.\n\n---\n\n## 2. On-Disk File Structure and Naming\n\n### Directory Layout Per Cache\n\n```\n<Application Support>/DiskCache/<CacheName>/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ index.json          # Persisted LRU index\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ entries/\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ a3f1b2c4        # Raw file content, named by hashed key\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ 9e0d7f11\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ ...\n```\n\n- Base directory: `FileManager.default.urls(for: .applicationSupportDirectory, in: .userDomainMask).first`\n- Each named cache gets its own subdirectory: `DiskCache/<name>/entries/`\n- The index lives at `DiskCache/<name>/index.json`\n- The `tmp/` eviction destination is `FileManager.default.temporaryDirectory`\n\n### File Naming Scheme for Entries\n\nKeys are arbitrary strings (e.g. URLs, UUIDs). Rather than storing them verbatim (which risks path-separator injection and length issues), each key is hashed:\n\n```\nfilename = SHA256(key.utf8).hexString.prefix(16)\n```\n\nUsing 16 hex characters (64-bit prefix of SHA-256) gives negligible collision probability for practical cache sizes. Full SHA-256 is computed and stored in the index for collision detection. On a filename collision the entry is treated as a separate bucket with the full hash as the tiebreaker.\n\nNo file extensions are used. The index records the original key, so lookup is always index-first, never filesystem-scan-based.\n\n### Eviction Move-to-tmp Naming\n\nWhen a file is evicted it is moved to `tmp/` with a collision-safe name:\n\n```\n<original-filename>-<UUID().uuidString>\n```\n\nThe UUID suffix guarantees uniqueness in `tmp/` regardless of prior evictions.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Types, Structs, Actors and Their Responsibilities\n\n### `CacheConfiguration` (struct, public)\n\nA value type. All fields have defaults so callers can use partial initialization via an initializer or a builder-style API.\n\nFields:\n- `name: String` ‚Äî namespace on disk\n- `maxEntryCount: Int` ‚Äî e.g. 1000; 0 means unlimited\n- `maxTotalBytes: Int` ‚Äî e.g. 500 MB; 0 means unlimited\n- `evictionDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` ‚Äî default 2.0 s\n- `indexSaveDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` ‚Äî default 5.0 s (for get/promote)\n- `dataProtectionClass: DataProtectionClass` ‚Äî enum, default `.completeUnlessOpen`\n\n```swift\npublic enum DataProtectionClass {\n    case none\n    case complete\n    case completeUnlessOpen\n    case completeUntilFirstUserAuthentication\n}\n```\n\n### `CacheError` (enum, public, Error)\n\n```swift\npublic enum CacheError: Error {\n    case keyNotFound(String)\n    case fileSystemError(underlying: Error)\n    case indexCorrupted\n    case atomicWriteFailed(underlying: Error)\n    case directoryCreationFailed(underlying: Error)\n}\n```\n\nThe `keyNotFound` case is what `modify` and `promote` throw when the key is absent.\n\n### `CacheEntry` (struct, internal, Codable)\n\nThis is the per-entry record stored inside the index. It is the single source of truth for LRU metadata.\n\nFields:\n- `key: String` ‚Äî original caller key\n- `filename: String` ‚Äî derived on-disk name (16-hex SHA-256 prefix)\n- `fullHash: String` ‚Äî full 64-hex SHA-256, for collision detection\n- `byteSize: Int` ‚Äî byte count of the stored payload\n- `lastAccessedDate: Date` ‚Äî updated on get/promote/add/modify\n- `insertedDate: Date` ‚Äî immutable after creation\n\n### `CacheIndex` (struct, internal)\n\nThe in-memory representation of the index. Not itself an actor; it is a plain value type owned exclusively by `CacheActor`.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Maintains an ordered dictionary: `[String: CacheEntry]` keyed by the original cache key\n- Provides O(1) lookup by key\n- Provides O(n log n) LRU ordering when eviction needs a sorted list (n is bounded by maxEntryCount, so this is acceptable)\n- Tracks `totalBytes: Int` as a running sum, updated on insert/remove\n- Serializes/deserializes itself as `CacheIndexSnapshot` (Codable)\n\nInternal structure:\n\n```swift\nstruct CacheIndex {\n    private(set) var entries: [String: CacheEntry]  // keyed by original key\n    private(set) var totalBytes: Int\n\n    mutating func insert(_ entry: CacheEntry)\n    mutating func remove(key: String) -> CacheEntry?\n    mutating func touch(key: String, date: Date)   // update lastAccessedDate\n    func entriesSortedByLRU() -> [CacheEntry]      // ascending lastAccessedDate\n    func needsEviction(config: CacheConfiguration) -> Bool\n}\n```\n\n### `CacheIndexSnapshot` (struct, internal, Codable)\n\nThe on-disk serialization format. Kept separate from `CacheIndex` so the in-memory model can evolve independently.\n\nFields:\n- `version: Int` ‚Äî schema version, currently 1\n- `entries: [CacheEntry]`\n\nDecode: if `version` is unrecognized or JSON is malformed, return `nil` (graceful degradation).\n\n### `CacheActor` (actor, internal)\n\nThis is the heart of the implementation. All mutable state is owned here. It is `internal` because `DiskCache` is the public facade.\n\nState owned:\n- `var index: CacheIndex`\n- `let config: CacheConfiguration`\n- `let cacheDir: URL` ‚Äî entries directory\n- `let indexURL: URL`\n- `let evictionDebouncer: Debouncer`\n- `let indexSaveDebouncer: Debouncer`\n- `let fileProtection: FileProtectionMapper`\n\nMethods (all `async throws` unless noted):\n\n```swift\nfunc add(key: String, data: Data) async throws\nfunc update(key: String, data: Data) async throws\nfunc modify(key: String, data: Data) async throws   // throws .keyNotFound if absent\nfunc get(key: String) async throws -> Data?\nfunc promote(key: String) async throws              // throws .keyNotFound if absent\n```\n\nInternal helpers:\n\n```swift\nprivate func writeEntry(key: String, data: Data, isNew: Bool) async throws\nprivate func readPayload(for entry: CacheEntry) async throws -> Data?\nprivate func runEviction() async\nprivate func persistIndex(immediate: Bool) async\nprivate func ensureDirectoryExists() async throws\nprivate func moveToTmp(entry: CacheEntry) async\n```\n\n### `DiskCache` (struct or final class, public)\n\nThe public-facing type. Holds a reference to `CacheActor` internally. All public methods are `async throws` and simply forward to the actor.\n\nBecause actors enforce serial access, `DiskCache` itself needs no additional synchronization. It is a thin pass-through:\n\n```swift\npublic struct DiskCache: Sendable {\n    private let actor: CacheActor\n\n    public init(configuration: CacheConfiguration) async throws\n    public func add(key: String, data: Data) async throws\n    public func update(key: String, data: Data) async throws\n    public func modify(key: String, data: Data) async throws\n    public func get(key: String) async throws -> Data?\n    public func promote(key: String) async throws\n}\n```\n\n`DiskCache` is `Sendable` because `CacheActor` is an actor (actors are always `Sendable`).\n\n### `AtomicWriter` (struct, internal)\n\nStateless helper. One static method:\n\n```swift\nstruct AtomicWriter {\n    static func write(\n        _ data: Data,\n        to destination: URL,\n        dataProtection: URLFileProtection,\n        fileManager: FileManager = .default\n    ) throws\n}\n```\n\nAlgorithm described in section 4.\n\n### `Debouncer` (actor, internal)\n\nA generic debounce mechanism backed by a `Task`. Described in section 4.\n\n### `FileProtectionMapper` (enum, internal)\n\nMaps `DataProtectionClass` to `URLFileProtection`:\n\n```swift\nenum FileProtectionMapper {\n    static func urlProtection(for class: DataProtectionClass) -> URLFileProtection\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Key Algorithms\n\n### 4a. LRU Eviction Logic\n\nEviction is triggered inside `CacheActor` after every mutation (`add`, `modify`) using the debouncer. The `runEviction()` method:\n\n1. Check `index.needsEviction(config: config)`. If false, return.\n2. Call `index.entriesSortedByLRU()` ‚Äî ascending `lastAccessedDate`, so index 0 is the stalest.\n3. Iterate from index 0 upward, collecting entries to evict until both constraints are satisfied:\n   - `index.entries.count <= config.maxEntryCount`\n   - `index.totalBytes <= config.maxTotalBytes`\n4. For each entry to evict:\n   a. Call `moveToTmp(entry:)`.\n   b. Call `index.remove(key: entry.key)`.\n5. After all evictions, call `persistIndex(immediate: true)`.\n\n`moveToTmp(entry:)`:\n1. Construct source URL: `cacheDir/<entry.filename>`\n2. Construct destination URL: `FileManager.temporaryDirectory/<entry.filename>-<UUID>`\n3. Call `FileManager.default.moveItem(at:to:)`.\n4. Silently ignore `NSFileNoSuchFileError` ‚Äî the file may have been deleted externally.\n\nThe eviction loop is O(n log n) for the sort, O(k) for the eviction walk where k is entries evicted. For practical cache sizes (< 10,000 entries) this is fast enough to run entirely inside the actor.\n\n### 4b. Atomic Write Mechanism\n\niOS does not provide a kernel-level atomic rename to a specific path in one syscall from Swift, but the `write-to-tmp-then-rename` pattern is the standard approach and is safe on the same filesystem volume:\n\n```\nAtomicWriter.write(data, to: destination):\n1. Generate tmpURL = destination.deletingLastPathComponent()\n                      .appendingPathComponent(UUID().uuidString + \".tmp\")\n2. Write data to tmpURL with options: [.atomic] ‚Äî no, use direct write here:\n   data.write(to: tmpURL, options: []) \n   // .atomic on the write itself would double-tmp; write directly to our tmp path\n3. Apply file protection attribute to tmpURL via FileManager.setAttributes\n4. Rename: FileManager.default.moveItem(at: tmpURL, to: destination)\n   // moveItem is atomic on same volume on iOS (POSIX rename under the hood)\n5. On any error: attempt cleanup of tmpURL, rethrow wrapped in .atomicWriteFailed\n```\n\nNote: `Data.write(options: .atomic)` uses its own internal temp file, which doesn't allow setting protection class before the rename. Writing to an explicit tmp URL first, setting attributes, then renaming gives full control.\n\nThe tmp file for the atomic write lives in the same directory as the destination (`entries/`), guaranteeing same-volume semantics for `moveItem`.\n\n### 4c. Eviction Debounce Mechanism\n\n`Debouncer` is an `actor` that owns a `Task?`. The debounce pattern:\n\n```swift\nactor Debouncer {\n    private var pendingTask: Task<Void, Never>?\n    private let interval: TimeInterval\n\n    func schedule(work: @escaping @Sendable () async -> Void) {\n        pendingTask?.cancel()\n        pendingTask = Task {\n            try? await Task.sleep(nanoseconds: UInt64(interval * 1_000_000_000))\n            guard !Task.isCancelled else { return }\n            await work()\n        }\n    }\n\n    func fireNow() {\n        pendingTask?.cancel()\n        pendingTask = nil\n    }\n}\n```\n\nEviction debounce: after each mutation, `CacheActor` calls `evictionDebouncer.schedule { await self.runEviction() }`. If another mutation arrives within the interval, the prior eviction task is cancelled and a new one is scheduled. This coalesces rapid burst writes into a single eviction pass.\n\n### 4d. Index Persistence Debounce\n\nA second `Debouncer` instance (`indexSaveDebouncer`) is used for get/promote. These operations update `lastAccessedDate` in the in-memory index immediately but defer the disk write:\n\n- `get`/`promote`: call `indexSaveDebouncer.schedule { await self.persistIndex(immediate: false) }`\n- `add`/`modify`/`runEviction`: call `persistIndex(immediate: true)` directly (no debounce), and also call `indexSaveDebouncer.fireNow()` to cancel any pending debounced save (the immediate save supersedes it)\n\n`persistIndex(immediate: Bool)` simply serializes `CacheIndex` to JSON and calls `AtomicWriter.write` to `indexURL`.\n\n### 4e. Init Sequence (Fast Start)\n\nThe `DiskCache` initializer is `async throws`:\n\n1. Construct `cacheDir` and `indexURL` from config name.\n2. Attempt to read and decode `index.json`. If missing or corrupt, start with an empty `CacheIndex` (no throw, just log if a logger is injected).\n3. Set up `Debouncer` instances.\n4. Return. No blocking I/O on the hot path ‚Äî the index load in step 2 happens once at init time in the async context, which is acceptable since the caller `await`s it.\n\nThe key property is that after init completes, all subsequent reads and writes are non-blocking relative to the caller: they hop to the actor's executor, do their work, and return. There is no synchronous disk I/O on the main thread.\n\n### 4f. Self-Healing on Missing File at `get` Time\n\nInside `CacheActor.get(key:)`:\n\n```\n1. Look up entry in index. If absent ‚Üí return nil.\n2. Attempt to read data from cacheDir/<entry.filename>.\n3. If file not found (catch NSCocoaErrorDomain NSFileReadNoSuchFileError):\n   a. index.remove(key: key)\n   b. persistIndex(immediate: true)\n   c. return nil\n4. Otherwise return data and update lastAccessedDate + schedule index save debounce.\n```\n\n### 4g. Directory Recreation\n\n`ensureDirectoryExists()` is called at the start of every write operation (`add`, `modify`, `runEviction`):\n\n```swift\nprivate func ensureDirectoryExists() async throws {\n    guard !FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: cacheDir.path) else { return }\n    do {\n        try FileManager.default.createDirectory(\n            at: cacheDir,\n            withIntermediateDirectories: true,\n            attributes: [.protectionKey: fileProtection]\n        )\n    } catch {\n        throw CacheError.directoryCreationFailed(underlying: error)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis is called inside the actor, so it is serial and safe.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Index Data Model (Fields Per Entry)\n\nStored in `index.json` as a JSON array of objects:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"https://example.com/image.png\",\n      \"filename\": \"a3f1b2c4d5e6f708\",\n      \"fullHash\": \"a3f1b2c4d5e6f708...64hexchars...\",\n      \"byteSize\": 204800,\n      \"lastAccessedDate\": 756864000.0,\n      \"insertedDate\": 756777600.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`lastAccessedDate` and `insertedDate` are stored as `TimeInterval` (seconds since reference date, i.e. `Date.timeIntervalSinceReferenceDate`). Using `TimeInterval` avoids ISO-8601 string parsing overhead and is unambiguous.\n\nThe `version` field allows future schema migrations: if `version > 1`, the decoder can choose to either migrate or discard the index gracefully.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Concurrency Model in Detail\n\n### Actor Isolation\n\n`CacheActor` is a Swift `actor`. This means:\n\n- All stored properties (`index`, `config`, `cacheDir`, debouncers) are actor-isolated.\n- All methods are implicitly `async` when called from outside the actor.\n- The actor's serial executor ensures that no two operations run concurrently within the actor, eliminating data races on the index without explicit locking.\n\n### What Runs on Which Executor\n\n| Operation | Executor |\n|---|---|\n| `DiskCache.init` | Caller's async context; index load is awaited |\n| `add/update/modify/get/promote` | CacheActor's serial executor |\n| `AtomicWriter.write` (disk I/O) | CacheActor's serial executor (blocking call; acceptable since actor uses cooperative thread pool) |\n| `runEviction` | CacheActor's serial executor (scheduled via Debouncer Task) |\n| `Debouncer.schedule` | Debouncer actor's executor (hop cost is minimal) |\n| `Task.sleep` inside Debouncer | Cooperative thread pool, does not block any thread |\n\n### Why Not a Serial DispatchQueue\n\nSwift actors on iOS 16+ integrate with the Swift concurrency runtime's cooperative thread pool. Using `DispatchQueue.main.async` or a serial background queue would require bridging with `withCheckedContinuation`, adding complexity. An actor is the idiomatic and safer choice under strict concurrency checking.\n\n### File I/O and Blocking\n\n`FileManager` calls (read, write, move) are blocking. Running them inside an actor on the cooperative thread pool is technically a concern for thread pool exhaustion under heavy concurrent load. For a cache serving a single app, this is not a real concern. If desired in future, I/O could be offloaded with `Task.detached { ... }` and results returned to the actor, but that adds complexity without material benefit for the target use case.\n\n### Sendability\n\n- `DiskCache` is `Sendable` (actor-backed).\n- `CacheConfiguration` is `Sendable` (all fields are value types).\n- `Data` is `Sendable`.\n- `CacheEntry` and `CacheIndex` are `Sendable` (pure value types).\n- `Debouncer` is an actor, therefore `Sendable`.\n\n### Preventing Index Races Between Debounced Save and Immediate Save\n\nBecause both the debounced index save and the immediate index save run on the `CacheActor`'s serial executor, they cannot interleave. The `fireNow()` call on the debouncer cancels the pending `Task`, and the subsequent immediate save runs atomically from the actor's perspective. No additional coordination is needed.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Test Strategy\n\n### Framework\n\nUse **Swift Testing** (introduced in Swift 5.9, available on iOS 17+ and macOS 14+). For targets needing iOS 16 compatibility, fall back to XCTest. Given this is a fresh package with a modern toolchain, Swift Testing is the right choice.\n\n### Test Helper: `TestCacheFactory`\n\n```swift\nstruct TestCacheFactory {\n    static func make(\n        name: String = UUID().uuidString,\n        maxEntryCount: Int = 100,\n        maxTotalBytes: Int = 10 * 1024 * 1024,\n        evictionDebounce: TimeInterval = 0.0,  // 0 = fire immediately for tests\n        indexSaveDebounce: TimeInterval = 0.0\n    ) async throws -> (DiskCache, URL) {\n        // Returns cache + its directory for inspection/cleanup\n    }\n\n    static func cleanup(at url: URL) throws { ... }\n}\n```\n\nSetting debounce intervals to 0 in tests eliminates the need for `Task.sleep` waits in test assertions.\n\n### Test Files and Coverage\n\n**`DiskCacheTests.swift`**\n- `add` inserts and `get` retrieves correctly\n- `update` replaces existing entry\n- `modify` succeeds when key exists\n- `modify` throws `.keyNotFound` when key absent\n- `get` returns `nil` for unknown key\n- `promote` throws `.keyNotFound` when key absent\n- `get` and `promote` update `lastAccessedDate`\n\n**`EvictionTests.swift`**\n- Inserting beyond `maxEntryCount` evicts LRU entry\n- Inserting beyond `maxTotalBytes` evicts LRU entries until under limit\n- Evicted entry file moved to `tmp/`, not deleted\n- Eviction does not evict most-recently-used entry\n- After eviction, `get` on evicted key returns `nil`\n- Multiple simultaneous rapid inserts trigger single eviction pass (debounce test with short interval)\n\n**`PersistenceTests.swift`**\n- Index survives process restart: create cache, add entries, reinitialize `DiskCache` from same directory, verify entries present\n- Corrupted `index.json` causes graceful degradation to empty cache, not crash\n- Missing `index.json` on init produces empty cache\n- LRU order is restored from persisted index (not reset on reinit)\n\n**`ConcurrencyTests.swift`**\n- Concurrent `add` calls from multiple tasks do not corrupt index (check `totalBytes` invariant)\n- Concurrent `get` and `add` do not produce torn reads\n- Use Swift Testing's `withTaskGroup` to issue parallel operations\n\n**`AtomicWriterTests.swift`**\n- Write succeeds and file appears at destination\n- Partial write (simulated by making destination directory unwritable) leaves no tmp file behind\n- Overwrite of existing file is atomic (no window where file is absent)\n\n**`Helpers/TestCacheFactory.swift`**\n- Factory and cleanup utilities\n- `@Suite(.serialized)` annotation on suites that manipulate the filesystem, to prevent parallel test runs from colliding on shared paths\n\n### Test Isolation\n\nEach test creates its cache in a unique subdirectory (using `UUID` as the cache name), so tests are fully independent and can be parallelized at the suite level.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Summary of Design Decisions\n\n| Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| Concurrency primitive | Swift `actor` | Native to Swift concurrency, zero-overhead serial execution, eliminates locks |\n| Index format | JSON via `Codable` | Human-readable, easy to version, no binary dependency |\n| Atomic write | Write to sibling `.tmp` file, then `FileManager.moveItem` (POSIX rename) | Same-volume rename is atomic on iOS APFS |\n| File naming | 16-hex SHA-256 prefix of key | Avoids path injection, handles arbitrary key strings, short enough for APFS |\n| Eviction debounce | `actor Debouncer` with `Task.cancel` + `Task.sleep` | Pure Swift concurrency, no GCD dependency |\n| Index save debounce | Second `Debouncer` instance with shorter interval | Separates mutation-triggered (immediate) from access-triggered (debounced) saves |\n| Eviction destination | `FileManager.temporaryDirectory` with UUID suffix | Satisfies requirement, handles collisions, OS manages tmp cleanup |\n| Data protection | Applied via `FileManager.setAttributes` on tmp file before rename | Ensures protection class is set before file is visible at destination path |\n| Error model | `CacheError` enum with associated values | Caller can pattern-match without stringly-typed catches |\n| Fast start | Index loaded once in `async init`; no blocking on subsequent calls | Actor serializes all subsequent I/O without blocking callers |\n| Graceful corruption | Decode returns `nil` ‚Üí fall back to empty `CacheIndex` | Never crash on bad data; cache is a performance layer, not source of truth |\n\n---\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n\n- `/workspace/Sources/DiskCache/CacheActor.swift`\n- `/workspace/Sources/DiskCache/CacheIndex.swift`\n- `/workspace/Sources/DiskCache/AtomicWriter.swift`\n- `/workspace/Sources/DiskCache/Debouncer.swift`\n- `/workspace/Package.swift`"}]}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SjUeTrUbo6jDSNraJbN31W","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/root/.claude/plans/cuddly-bubbling-whale.md","content":"# LRU Disk Cache ‚Äî Swift Implementation Plan\n\n## Context\n\nGreenfield iOS Swift Package implementing a disk-backed LRU file cache. The workspace is empty. The cache must support multiple independent named instances, survive restarts, evict asynchronously without blocking callers, and expose a clear async/throws API. All requirements come from the spec in the conversation.\n\n---\n\n## Package Structure\n\n```\nDiskCache/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Package.swift\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Sources/DiskCache/\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCache.swift           # Public facade (struct, Sendable)\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheConfiguration.swift  # Config value type + DataProtectionClass enum\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheError.swift          # Public error enum\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheActor.swift          # Internal actor ‚Äî owns all mutable state\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheIndex.swift          # In-memory index (value type) + Codable snapshot\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheEntry.swift          # Per-entry metadata (Codable struct)\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriter.swift        # Static helper: write-to-tmp + rename\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Debouncer.swift           # Generic actor-based debounce\n‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ FileProtectionMapper.swift # Maps DataProtectionClass ‚Üí URLFileProtection\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Tests/DiskCacheTests/\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCacheTests.swift       # Core API tests\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ EvictionTests.swift        # LRU ordering + eviction tests\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ PersistenceTests.swift     # Index survives restart + corruption recovery\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ ConcurrencyTests.swift     # Race safety\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriterTests.swift    # Atomic write correctness\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Helpers/TestCacheFactory.swift\n```\n\n**`Package.swift`**: swift-tools-version 5.9, platform iOS 16+, strict concurrency enabled, one library target + one test target.\n\n---\n\n## On-Disk Layout (per cache named `<N>`)\n\n```\n<AppSupport>/DiskCache/<N>/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ index.json      # Persisted LRU index\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ entries/\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ <16-hex>    # Raw payload, named SHA-256(key).prefix(16)\n```\n\nEvicted files move to `FileManager.temporaryDirectory/<filename>-<UUID>` (UUID prevents collisions).\n\n---\n\n## Types\n\n### `CacheConfiguration` (public struct, Sendable)\n- `name: String`\n- `maxEntryCount: Int` (0 = unlimited)\n- `maxTotalBytes: Int` (0 = unlimited)\n- `evictionDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` (default 2.0)\n- `indexSaveDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` (default 5.0)\n- `dataProtectionClass: DataProtectionClass` (default `.completeUnlessOpen`)\n\n### `DataProtectionClass` (public enum, Sendable)\n`.none | .complete | .completeUnlessOpen | .completeUntilFirstUserAuthentication`\n\n### `CacheError` (public enum: Error)\n`.keyNotFound(String) | .fileSystemError(Error) | .atomicWriteFailed(Error) | .directoryCreationFailed(Error) | .indexCorrupted`\n\n### `CacheEntry` (internal struct, Codable, Sendable)\n`key, filename, fullHash, byteSize: Int, lastAccessedDate: Date, insertedDate: Date`\n\n### `CacheIndex` (internal struct, Sendable)\n- Owns `[String: CacheEntry]` + `totalBytes: Int`\n- `mutating insert/remove/touch`\n- `entriesSortedByLRU() -> [CacheEntry]` (ascending lastAccessedDate)\n- `needsEviction(config:) -> Bool`\n- Serializes via `CacheIndexSnapshot` (versioned Codable wrapper, version=1)\n\n### `CacheActor` (internal actor)\nOwns: `index: CacheIndex`, `config`, `cacheDir`, `indexURL`, `evictionDebouncer`, `indexSaveDebouncer`\n\nPublic-forwarded methods: `add`, `update`, `modify`, `get`, `promote`\n\nPrivate helpers: `writeEntry`, `readPayload`, `runEviction`, `persistIndex(immediate:)`, `ensureDirectoryExists`, `moveToTmp`\n\n### `DiskCache` (public struct, Sendable)\nThin pass-through holding a `CacheActor` reference. All methods `async throws`. `init(configuration:)` is `async throws` (loads index).\n\n### `AtomicWriter` (internal struct)\n```swift\nstatic func write(_ data: Data, to: URL, protection: URLFileProtection) throws\n```\nAlgorithm: write to sibling `.tmp` file ‚Üí set protection attributes ‚Üí `FileManager.moveItem` (POSIX rename, atomic same-volume).\n\n### `Debouncer` (internal actor)\nCancels prior `Task`, schedules new `Task.sleep` + work closure. `fireNow()` cancels pending task (used before immediate saves).\n\n---\n\n## Key Algorithms\n\n### Init (Fast Start)\n1. Derive `cacheDir` + `indexURL` from config name\n2. Attempt decode of `index.json`; on missing/corrupt ‚Üí empty `CacheIndex` (no throw)\n3. Create debouncer instances\n4. Return ‚Äî no blocking I/O after init completes\n\n### `add` / `update`\n1. `ensureDirectoryExists()`\n2. Compute SHA-256(key); derive filename (first 16 hex chars)\n3. `AtomicWriter.write` to `entries/<filename>`\n4. `index.insert(entry)` (upsert ‚Äî replaces if key exists)\n5. `persistIndex(immediate: true)` + cancel indexSaveDebouncer\n6. Schedule eviction debouncer\n\n### `modify`\nSame as `add` but step 4 checks key exists first ‚Äî throws `.keyNotFound` if absent.\n\n### `get`\n1. Look up entry in index ‚Üí nil if absent\n2. Read file from `entries/<filename>`; if file missing ‚Üí remove from index, `persistIndex(immediate: true)`, return nil\n3. `index.touch(key, date: .now)`\n4. Schedule `indexSaveDebouncer`\n5. Return data\n\n### `promote`\n1. Look up entry ‚Üí throw `.keyNotFound` if absent\n2. `index.touch(key, date: .now)`\n3. Schedule `indexSaveDebouncer`\n\n### Eviction (`runEviction`)\n1. Check `index.needsEviction(config:)` ‚Üí return if not needed\n2. `index.entriesSortedByLRU()` (ascending = LRU first)\n3. Walk from index 0, collect entries to evict until both constraints satisfied\n4. For each: `moveToTmp` ‚Üí `index.remove`\n5. `persistIndex(immediate: true)`\n\n### `moveToTmp(entry:)`\n`FileManager.moveItem(at: cacheDir/<filename>, to: tmp/<filename>-<UUID>)`. Ignore `NSFileNoSuchFileError` silently.\n\n### Index Persistence\n- **Immediate** (mutations + eviction): serialize `CacheIndex` to JSON, `AtomicWriter.write` to `indexURL`, cancel `indexSaveDebouncer`\n- **Debounced** (get/promote): `indexSaveDebouncer.schedule { persistIndex(immediate: false) }`\n\n### Directory Recreation\n`ensureDirectoryExists()` called at the top of every write. Creates `entries/` dir with protection attributes if absent.\n\n---\n\n## Concurrency Model\n\n- `CacheActor` serial executor serializes all state mutations ‚Äî no locks needed\n- `Debouncer` is also an actor; hop cost is negligible\n- Both debouncers run on the cooperative thread pool via `Task.sleep + cancel`\n- File I/O runs on the actor's executor; acceptable for single-app workloads\n- All public types conform to `Sendable`\n\n---\n\n## Index JSON Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"https://example.com/img.png\",\n      \"filename\": \"a3f1b2c4d5e6f708\",\n      \"fullHash\": \"<64 hex chars>\",\n      \"byteSize\": 204800,\n      \"lastAccessedDate\": 756864000.0,\n      \"insertedDate\": 756777600.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nDates as `TimeInterval` (seconds since reference date). Unknown `version` ‚Üí graceful empty-cache fallback.\n\n---\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n**Framework**: Swift Testing (Swift 5.9+)\n\n`TestCacheFactory`: creates caches in unique temp subdirs, with debounce intervals set to `0` to eliminate async delays in tests.\n\n| File | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `DiskCacheTests` | add/get/update/modify/promote happy paths + error cases |\n| `EvictionTests` | LRU ordering, count/byte limits, evicted files in tmp, rapid-insert debounce |\n| `PersistenceTests` | Reinit restores index, corrupt JSON degrades to empty, missing index degrades to empty |\n| `ConcurrencyTests` | Concurrent adds don't corrupt totalBytes; concurrent get+add no torn reads |\n| `AtomicWriterTests` | Write produces correct file; failure leaves no tmp artifact; overwrite is atomic |\n\nEach test uses a UUID-named cache for full isolation.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n# Build\nswift build\n\n# Run all tests\nswift test\n\n# Verify no data races (if available)\nswift test --sanitize thread\n```\n\nFunctional smoke test: init cache, add 3 entries, reinit from same directory, verify all 3 accessible, verify LRU entry evicted after adding beyond maxEntryCount.\n"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SjUeTrUbo6jDSNraJbN31W","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /root/.claude/plans/cuddly-bubbling-whale.md"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UwY92ctNE7bPM2rvWqysyu","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"User has approved your plan. You can now start coding. Start with updating your todo list if applicable\n\nYour plan has been saved to: /root/.claude/plans/cuddly-bubbling-whale.md\nYou can refer back to it if needed during implementation.\n\n## Approved Plan:\n# LRU Disk Cache ‚Äî Swift Implementation Plan\n\n## Context\n\nGreenfield iOS Swift Package implementing a disk-backed LRU file cache. The workspace is empty. The cache must support multiple independent named instances, survive restarts, evict asynchronously without blocking callers, and expose a clear async/throws API. All requirements come from the spec in the conversation.\n\n---\n\n## Package Structure\n\n```\nDiskCache/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Package.swift\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Sources/DiskCache/\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCache.swift           # Public facade (struct, Sendable)\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheConfiguration.swift  # Config value type + DataProtectionClass enum\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheError.swift          # Public error enum\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheActor.swift          # Internal actor ‚Äî owns all mutable state\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheIndex.swift          # In-memory index (value type) + Codable snapshot\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ CacheEntry.swift          # Per-entry metadata (Codable struct)\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriter.swift        # Static helper: write-to-tmp + rename\n‚îÇ   ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ Debouncer.swift           # Generic actor-based debounce\n‚îÇ   ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ FileProtectionMapper.swift # Maps DataProtectionClass ‚Üí URLFileProtection\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Tests/DiskCacheTests/\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ DiskCacheTests.swift       # Core API tests\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ EvictionTests.swift        # LRU ordering + eviction tests\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ PersistenceTests.swift     # Index survives restart + corruption recovery\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ ConcurrencyTests.swift     # Race safety\n    ‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ AtomicWriterTests.swift    # Atomic write correctness\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ Helpers/TestCacheFactory.swift\n```\n\n**`Package.swift`**: swift-tools-version 5.9, platform iOS 16+, strict concurrency enabled, one library target + one test target.\n\n---\n\n## On-Disk Layout (per cache named `<N>`)\n\n```\n<AppSupport>/DiskCache/<N>/\n‚îú‚îÄ‚îÄ index.json      # Persisted LRU index\n‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ entries/\n    ‚îî‚îÄ‚îÄ <16-hex>    # Raw payload, named SHA-256(key).prefix(16)\n```\n\nEvicted files move to `FileManager.temporaryDirectory/<filename>-<UUID>` (UUID prevents collisions).\n\n---\n\n## Types\n\n### `CacheConfiguration` (public struct, Sendable)\n- `name: String`\n- `maxEntryCount: Int` (0 = unlimited)\n- `maxTotalBytes: Int` (0 = unlimited)\n- `evictionDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` (default 2.0)\n- `indexSaveDebounceInterval: TimeInterval` (default 5.0)\n- `dataProtectionClass: DataProtectionClass` (default `.completeUnlessOpen`)\n\n### `DataProtectionClass` (public enum, Sendable)\n`.none | .complete | .completeUnlessOpen | .completeUntilFirstUserAuthentication`\n\n### `CacheError` (public enum: Error)\n`.keyNotFound(String) | .fileSystemError(Error) | .atomicWriteFailed(Error) | .directoryCreationFailed(Error) | .indexCorrupted`\n\n### `CacheEntry` (internal struct, Codable, Sendable)\n`key, filename, fullHash, byteSize: Int, lastAccessedDate: Date, insertedDate: Date`\n\n### `CacheIndex` (internal struct, Sendable)\n- Owns `[String: CacheEntry]` + `totalBytes: Int`\n- `mutating insert/remove/touch`\n- `entriesSortedByLRU() -> [CacheEntry]` (ascending lastAccessedDate)\n- `needsEviction(config:) -> Bool`\n- Serializes via `CacheIndexSnapshot` (versioned Codable wrapper, version=1)\n\n### `CacheActor` (internal actor)\nOwns: `index: CacheIndex`, `config`, `cacheDir`, `indexURL`, `evictionDebouncer`, `indexSaveDebouncer`\n\nPublic-forwarded methods: `add`, `update`, `modify`, `get`, `promote`\n\nPrivate helpers: `writeEntry`, `readPayload`, `runEviction`, `persistIndex(immediate:)`, `ensureDirectoryExists`, `moveToTmp`\n\n### `DiskCache` (public struct, Sendable)\nThin pass-through holding a `CacheActor` reference. All methods `async throws`. `init(configuration:)` is `async throws` (loads index).\n\n### `AtomicWriter` (internal struct)\n```swift\nstatic func write(_ data: Data, to: URL, protection: URLFileProtection) throws\n```\nAlgorithm: write to sibling `.tmp` file ‚Üí set protection attributes ‚Üí `FileManager.moveItem` (POSIX rename, atomic same-volume).\n\n### `Debouncer` (internal actor)\nCancels prior `Task`, schedules new `Task.sleep` + work closure. `fireNow()` cancels pending task (used before immediate saves).\n\n---\n\n## Key Algorithms\n\n### Init (Fast Start)\n1. Derive `cacheDir` + `indexURL` from config name\n2. Attempt decode of `index.json`; on missing/corrupt ‚Üí empty `CacheIndex` (no throw)\n3. Create debouncer instances\n4. Return ‚Äî no blocking I/O after init completes\n\n### `add` / `update`\n1. `ensureDirectoryExists()`\n2. Compute SHA-256(key); derive filename (first 16 hex chars)\n3. `AtomicWriter.write` to `entries/<filename>`\n4. `index.insert(entry)` (upsert ‚Äî replaces if key exists)\n5. `persistIndex(immediate: true)` + cancel indexSaveDebouncer\n6. Schedule eviction debouncer\n\n### `modify`\nSame as `add` but step 4 checks key exists first ‚Äî throws `.keyNotFound` if absent.\n\n### `get`\n1. Look up entry in index ‚Üí nil if absent\n2. Read file from `entries/<filename>`; if file missing ‚Üí remove from index, `persistIndex(immediate: true)`, return nil\n3. `index.touch(key, date: .now)`\n4. Schedule `indexSaveDebouncer`\n5. Return data\n\n### `promote`\n1. Look up entry ‚Üí throw `.keyNotFound` if absent\n2. `index.touch(key, date: .now)`\n3. Schedule `indexSaveDebouncer`\n\n### Eviction (`runEviction`)\n1. Check `index.needsEviction(config:)` ‚Üí return if not needed\n2. `index.entriesSortedByLRU()` (ascending = LRU first)\n3. Walk from index 0, collect entries to evict until both constraints satisfied\n4. For each: `moveToTmp` ‚Üí `index.remove`\n5. `persistIndex(immediate: true)`\n\n### `moveToTmp(entry:)`\n`FileManager.moveItem(at: cacheDir/<filename>, to: tmp/<filename>-<UUID>)`. Ignore `NSFileNoSuchFileError` silently.\n\n### Index Persistence\n- **Immediate** (mutations + eviction): serialize `CacheIndex` to JSON, `AtomicWriter.write` to `indexURL`, cancel `indexSaveDebouncer`\n- **Debounced** (get/promote): `indexSaveDebouncer.schedule { persistIndex(immediate: false) }`\n\n### Directory Recreation\n`ensureDirectoryExists()` called at the top of every write. Creates `entries/` dir with protection attributes if absent.\n\n---\n\n## Concurrency Model\n\n- `CacheActor` serial executor serializes all state mutations ‚Äî no locks needed\n- `Debouncer` is also an actor; hop cost is negligible\n- Both debouncers run on the cooperative thread pool via `Task.sleep + cancel`\n- File I/O runs on the actor's executor; acceptable for single-app workloads\n- All public types conform to `Sendable`\n\n---\n\n## Index JSON Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"entries\": [\n    {\n      \"key\": \"https://example.com/img.png\",\n      \"filename\": \"a3f1b2c4d5e6f708\",\n      \"fullHash\": \"<64 hex chars>\",\n      \"byteSize\": 204800,\n      \"lastAccessedDate\": 756864000.0,\n      \"insertedDate\": 756777600.0\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nDates as `TimeInterval` (seconds since reference date). Unknown `version` ‚Üí graceful empty-cache fallback.\n\n---\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n**Framework**: Swift Testing (Swift 5.9+)\n\n`TestCacheFactory`: creates caches in unique temp subdirs, with debounce intervals set to `0` to eliminate async delays in tests.\n\n| File | Coverage |\n|---|---|\n| `DiskCacheTests` | add/get/update/modify/promote happy paths + error cases |\n| `EvictionTests` | LRU ordering, count/byte limits, evicted files in tmp, rapid-insert debounce |\n| `PersistenceTests` | Reinit restores index, corrupt JSON degrades to empty, missing index degrades to empty |\n| `ConcurrencyTests` | Concurrent adds don't corrupt totalBytes; concurrent get+add no torn reads |\n| `AtomicWriterTests` | Write produces correct file; failure leaves no tmp artifact; overwrite is atomic |\n\nEach test uses a UUID-named cache for full isolation.\n\n---\n\n## Verification\n\n```bash\n# Build\nswift build\n\n# Run all tests\nswift test\n\n# Verify no data races (if available)\nswift test --sanitize thread\n```\n\nFunctional smoke test: init cache, add 3 entries, reinit from same directory, verify all 3 accessible, verify LRU entry evicted after adding beyond maxEntryCount.\n\n<system-reminder>\n## Exited Plan Mode\n\nYou have exited plan mode. You can now make edits, run tools, and take actions. The plan file is located at /root/.claude/plans/cuddly-bubbling-whale.md if you need to reference it.\n</system-reminder>","tool_use_id":"toolu_01UwY92ctNE7bPM2rvWqysyu"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01STqwzPoUXwt7FfQwX8tcrS","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Create Package.swift and directory structure","description":"Create the Swift Package manifest and all source/test directories"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01STqwzPoUXwt7FfQwX8tcrS","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #1 created successfully: Create Package.swift and directory structure"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ve28cANLEfmH3SM3bLHgbv","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Implement core source files","description":"Write all Sources/DiskCache/*.swift files: CacheConfiguration, CacheError, CacheEntry, CacheIndex, AtomicWriter, Debouncer, FileProtectionMapper, CacheActor, DiskCache"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ve28cANLEfmH3SM3bLHgbv","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #2 created successfully: Implement core source files"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01V1TE4sZjZTpApzqAPxFHyT","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Implement test files","description":"Write all Tests/DiskCacheTests/*.swift files: TestCacheFactory, DiskCacheTests, EvictionTests, PersistenceTests, ConcurrencyTests, AtomicWriterTests"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V1TE4sZjZTpApzqAPxFHyT","type":"tool_result","content":"Task #3 created successfully: Implement test files"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Za1vCQJN9YbwvKYmXjHCC","name":"TaskCreate","input":{"subject":"Build and verify","description":"Run swift build and swift test to verify everything compiles and tests pass"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Za1vCQJN9YbwvKYmXjHCC","type":"tool_result","co